msgstr "[in] Absolute independent deadline, including policy delay."

msgid "Success, INVALID or STATE; no loan before successful begin."
msgstr "Success, INVALID or STATE; no loan before successful begin."

msgid "Prepare only the zero-data request's status-IN reply."
msgstr "Prepare only the zero-data request's status-IN reply."

msgid "Task-only. External standard-request policy must stage SET_ADDRESS itself and inspect authoritative address/closing state after wire ACK."
msgstr "Task-only. External standard-request policy must stage SET_ADDRESS itself and inspect authoritative address/closing state after wire ACK."

msgid "[in] Nonzero matching SETUP identity."
msgstr "[in] Nonzero matching SETUP identity."

msgid "[in] Absolute independent deadline."
msgstr "[in] Absolute independent deadline."

msgid "Success, INVALID or STATE; no transfer is started."
msgstr "Success, INVALID or STATE; no transfer is started."

msgid "Admit one explicit reply to the current authoritative SETUP epoch."
msgstr "Admit one explicit reply to the current authoritative SETUP epoch."

msgid "No packet is submitted by admission. Payload, request, profile and adapter remain alive until acquire-observed outer SETTLED. Never call prepare/reinitialize to revoke a loan. Epochs do not repeat. Products stage SET_ADDRESS explicitly; transport success means wire ACK only."
msgstr "No packet is submitted by admission. Payload, request, profile and adapter remain alive until acquire-observed outer SETTLED. Never call prepare/reinitialize to revoke a loan. Epochs do not repeat. Products stage SET_ADDRESS explicitly; transport success means wire ACK only."

msgid "[inout] Bound single-executor adapter; no other live reply."
msgstr "[inout] Bound single-executor adapter; no other live reply."

msgid "[inout] READY metadata and disjoint payload. OUT capacity must cover wLength; IN sends min(length,wLength), including required ZLP."
msgstr "[inout] READY metadata and disjoint payload. OUT capacity must cover wLength; IN sends min(length,wLength), including required ZLP."

msgid "Success means ACCEPTED; every failure retains no request or payload."
msgstr "Success means ACCEPTED; every failure retains no request or payload."

msgid "Make one bounded progress step, at most one poll and one packet action."
msgstr "Make one bounded progress step, at most one poll and one packet action."

msgid "No queue or worker. All packet deadlines use the outer independent absolute monotonic deadline. Poll while borrowed, even after cancel, reset, SETUP supersession or device stop. Cancel/drain/quarantine retain descriptor bytes and outer context. OUT0 quarantine exposes NEEDS_DEVICE_STOP; only the external controller owner may authorize stop. This adapter never stops the shared controller automatically. One SETTLED packet is folded before observing newer controller epochs."
msgstr "No queue or worker. All packet deadlines use the outer independent absolute monotonic deadline. Poll while borrowed, even after cancel, reset, SETUP supersession or device stop. Cancel/drain/quarantine retain descriptor bytes and outer context. OUT0 quarantine exposes NEEDS_DEVICE_STOP; only the external controller owner may authorize stop. This adapter never stops the shared controller automatically. One SETTLED packet is folded before observing newer controller epochs."

msgid "[inout] Same serialized executor and lifetime as begin."
msgstr "[inout] Same serialized executor and lifetime as begin."

msgid "Success or provider error; an error never revokes accepted storage."
msgstr "Success or provider error; an error never revokes accepted storage."

msgid "Request cancellation without revoking the old packet or outer loan."
msgstr "Request cancellation without revoking the old packet or outer loan."

msgid "An already acquired STATUS ACK wins. The next step issues at most one packet cancel; continue polling and retain quarantine until actual source withdrawal. OUT0 recovery may need explicit device-owner stop."
msgstr "An already acquired STATUS ACK wins. The next step issues at most one packet cancel; continue polling and retain quarantine until actual source withdrawal. OUT0 recovery may need explicit device-owner stop."

msgid "[inout] Same serialized privileged task executor."
msgstr "[inout] Same serialized privileged task executor."

msgid "[inout] Exact active outer request, kept alive until SETTLED."
msgstr "[inout] Exact active outer request, kept alive until SETTLED."

msgid "[in] Exact active SETUP identity; no cross-task raw pointer use."
msgstr "[in] Exact active SETUP identity; no cross-task raw pointer use."

msgid "Success requests drain; STATE rejects stale identity without effects."
msgstr "Success requests drain; STATE rejects stale identity without effects."

msgid "Inspect completed OUT DATA before the external policy approves STATUS."
msgstr "Inspect completed OUT DATA before the external policy approves STATUS."

msgid "The view expires at the next same-owner adapter call. No mutation, free, cross-task access or implicit status acknowledgement is allowed."
msgstr "The view expires at the next same-owner adapter call. No mutation, free, cross-task access or implicit status acknowledgement is allowed."

msgid "[in] DATA_READY with no provider packet references."
msgstr "[in] DATA_READY with no provider packet references."

msgid "[out] Disjoint value output, unchanged on rejection."
msgstr "[out] Disjoint value output, unchanged on rejection."

msgid "Success grants a const inspection view only; outer borrow continues."
msgstr "Success grants a const inspection view only; outer borrow continues."

msgid "Approve OUT policy before STATUS IN, or reject with a bounded STALL."
msgstr "Approve OUT policy before STATUS IN, or reject with a bounded STALL."

msgid "Bytes, class dispatch, configuration readiness and recovery policy are external. No CDC/HID stack is supplied. A guarded decision excludes an already software-published replacement SETUP. Physical bus packets not yet collected by IRQ are outside that software epoch boundary. Cancellation drains before the outer loan ends."
msgstr "Bytes, class dispatch, configuration readiness and recovery policy are external. No CDC/HID stack is supplied. A guarded decision excludes an already software-published replacement SETUP. Physical bus packets not yet collected by IRQ are outside that software epoch boundary. Cancellation drains before the outer loan ends."

msgid "[inout] DATA_READY same-owner adapter."
msgstr "[inout] DATA_READY same-owner adapter."

msgid "[in] Exact active SETUP epoch, checked against fresh state."
msgstr "[in] Exact active SETUP epoch, checked against fresh state."

msgid "[in] True permits status; false stalls the old transaction."
msgstr "[in] True permits status; false stalls the old transaction."

msgid "Success changes policy only; the next step performs packet/STALL."
msgstr "Success changes policy only; the next step performs packet/STALL."

msgid "Copy the last acquired authoritative state and adapter phase."
msgstr "Copy the last acquired authoritative state and adapter phase."

msgid "Call step to refresh controller state. Wire success does not imply address/configuration readiness. Snapshots never release a loan."
msgstr "Call step to refresh controller state. Wire success does not imply address/configuration readiness. Snapshots never release a loan."

msgid "[in] Same single task executor; no provider operation occurs."
msgstr "[in] Same single task executor; no provider operation occurs."

msgid "Success, INVALID or CONTEXT."
msgstr "Success, INVALID or CONTEXT."

msgid "Adapter-private fields, caller-owned and fixed capacity."
msgstr "Adapter-private fields, caller-owned and fixed capacity."

msgid "Public context/request/output metadata require natural C alignment and nonwrapping extents. Misalignment is INVALID before typed access. Pointers still require documented readable/writable storage: numeric checks cannot validate arbitrary address maps or opaque private provider contexts."
msgstr "Public context/request/output metadata require natural C alignment and nonwrapping extents. Misalignment is INVALID before typed access. Pointers still require documented readable/writable storage: numeric checks cannot validate arbitrary address maps or opaque private provider contexts."

